# .gitignore — SSM RISC-V Extension
#
# Rule for adding anything here: could I regenerate this exactly, from something
# that IS committed? If yes, ignore it — and make sure the generating script is
# committed too.
#
# The deliberate exception: generated files that are the EVIDENCE for a claim
# (exported weights, golden vectors that passed a hardware gate) get committed,
# because "regenerate it from a checkpoint that isn't in the repo" is not
# reproducible. Those are listed as negations at the bottom.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Obsidian — per-machine editor config, not part of the project.
# Ignored wholesale: app/appearance/core-plugins are personal settings and
# themes/ carries a 40 KB CSS. The vault still works locally; nothing here is
# needed to build or reproduce the project.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.obsidian/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vivado (Stage 1 onward)
#
# Project mode keeps state in .runs/.cache/.sim, which regenerate from the
# sources. The .xpr and your .sv/.xdc are the real content. These directories
# reach several GB, so this block matters more than any other.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.cache/
*.hw/
*.ip_user_files/
*.runs/
*.sim/
*.gen/
.Xil/
*.jou
*.log
*.str
*.wdb
*.pb
vivado_pid*
hs_err_pid*

# Non-project build outputs (Stage 5, scripts/build.tcl)
build/

# GUI project, if you generate one from a script (scripts/create_gui_project.tcl)
vivado_gui/

# Vivado byproduct: re-dirties on every build and describes design_1, not this
# design. If it ever gets committed by accident: git rm --cached clockInfo.txt
clockInfo.txt

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Firmware (Stage 3 onward) — all regenerate with fw/build.sh
#
# Keep the SOURCES (crt0.S, main.c, link.ld, build.sh) and drop the outputs.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
fw/*.elf
fw/*.bin
fw/*.o
fw/*.map
fw/*.dis
fw/*.mem
fw/build_info.txt

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Upstream RISC-V core (Stage 4)
#
# Cloned, not vendored into history. This is only safe to ignore because
# scripts/fetch_core.sh pins the exact revision — if that script is missing or
# unpinned, this line is reckless rather than clean.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
vendor/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Measurement outputs (Stage 5)
#
# Timestamped, and every file carries its own .meta with git rev and compiler
# flags. Attach the specific captures that back a headline claim to a GitHub
# Release instead of committing them.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
results/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Python model development (Stage 6 onward)
#
# venv is bootstrapped (see py/README.md); MIT-BIH is re-downloadable from
# PhysioNet (~90 MB); checkpoints are large and regenerable from train.py.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
py/venv/
py/data/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Large generated host-test vectors (regenerate: py/export_c.py --host-beats)
py/golden_host.h

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Editor / OS noise
#
# Personal preferences belong in ~/.gitignore_global, not here — a project
# .gitignore should describe the PROJECT, so it makes sense to a collaborator.
# These few are common enough to be worth catching locally.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*~
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deliberate exceptions — generated, but committed as EVIDENCE
#
# These are the exact artefacts behind hardware claims. Regenerating them
# depends on a checkpoint in py/data/, which is ignored — so committing them is
# what makes a "bit-exact on hardware" claim reproducible.
#
# NOTE: as written, these two negations are no-ops — nothing above ignores .h
# files in fw/ (only .elf/.bin/.o/.map/.dis/.mem). They are here as a statement
# of intent, and as insurance if a broader rule like `fw/*` is ever added.
# Verify with:  git check-ignore -q fw/golden.h ; echo $?     # 1 = not ignored
#
# If you do add a broader rule, it must come BEFORE these lines: last match wins,
# and a negation cannot rescue a file inside an already-excluded *directory*.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
!fw/golden.h
!fw/model_data.h
